<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="d89bc142">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify the key users to carry out UAT testing.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Train&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;UAT testers&amp;nbsp;in the following areas: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Testing cycle expectations (e.g., how to run an acceptable test and record your results, screenshots,
                document numbers, how to record defects, where hardware (e.g., printers, RF guns, wedge scanners, etc.) is
                available
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Who are the key contacts for questions
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Basic system behavior (e.g., &amp;nbsp;logging on, navigation, shortcuts, common display elements, user
                interface display customizing, etc.)
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Set expectations of system data, configuration and development that will impact testing, by communicating: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                What master data is available
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Development that is not complete
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Any work that has been postponed by project management as &quot;post go-live&quot;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="7d4f7681"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="5bda280c">&lt;p&gt;
    UAT testers should be trained on basic system capability and test process expectations so that the focus can be on
    consistently testing whether the system design meets the stakeholder requirements and is not derailed by &quot;new user&quot;
    issues.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Each functional team should train their key users separately on the &quot;big picture&quot; processes&amp;nbsp;for which they
    responsible&amp;nbsp;and the key users will be testing.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="9b26d24"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="94119039">To verify that business users are identified, engaged, and committed to participate.&amp;nbsp;With this assurance, conflicts
can be minimized, and the test cycles can be completed as smoothly as possible.&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
